  "description": "*“If I could go back in time, I wouldn’t have fallen in love with him.”*\n\nAfter returning to the past, her second marriage to her ex-husband was solely for the sake of her child. Unlike her previous life, where she had yearned for love, this second life—gained as if by a miracle— led her to choose marriage to him with the single-minded determination to reunite with her child.\n\n *“Just keep up the pretense of our marriage for exactly one year.”*\n\nThe price she paid was to cooperate with him in uncovering the secret behind the incident from ten years ago, just as he wished. She thought they were just a couple in name only, bound by that contract… \n\n *“We don’t necessarily have to spend our wedding night together—”\n\n“I want to.”*\n\nHe was different from her past life.\n\n(Source: Naver, translated)",
